				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1861,
				2
			],
			"Message": "docs(Mountain): Add rustdoc comments to TerminalEnvCollection and polish Initialize docs\n\nAdd doc comments with variant/field descriptions to `MutatorType`, `Mutator`, and `ExtensionCollection` types in `TerminalEnvCollection`, and to the `Replace` free function. These types manage environment variable mutations registered by extensions, mirroring VS Code's `EnvironmentVariableMutatorType`.\n\nRewrite the `Initialize` module doc to be more concise: replace the section-title header with a direct `//!` summary, tighten the lifecycle section, and fix several half-edited doc phrases that were left in a transitional state from an earlier rewrite pass.",
			"SHA": "24c3dc016be753a6999cb668743cacad67fbcddb"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T19:12:16Z",
			"File": [
				"⡟⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1861,
				300
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Wire bidirectional Vine streaming multiplexer and expand Sky replay coverage\n\nImplement `open_channel_from_cocoon` on `MountainVinegRPCService`, enabling bidirectional streaming between Cocoon and Mountain over the Vine protocol. The read pump dispatches inbound `Envelope` frames through the same paths as their unary counterparts (notification → send_cocoon_notification, request → process_cocoon_request, cancel → cancel_operation) and pushes responses back via `CHANNEL_REGISTRY`. A `ChannelId` field on `Envelope` lets receivers detect stale pre-reconnect frames.\n\nExpand `sky:replay-events` to rebuild output channels (create + buffered content, capped at 200 lines per channel), diagnostics markers per owner, and status bar entries — filling gaps where late SkyBridge listeners missed state that settled before boot. Add `language:cancelRequest` forwarding to Cocoon so the workbench can abort in-flight provider calls.\n\nRefactor both GenericNotification and GenericRequest dispatchers: Sky-emit handlers resolve through a `Lazy<HashMap>` lookup (eliminating sequential string matching); GenericRequest methods dispatch through a `Route` enum backed by a `HashMap`. Output channel state (name, buffer, visibility) is now tracked in `ApplicationState.Feature.OutputChannels` at every append/create/clear/show/dispose site, enabling the replay path and consistent visibility through Cocoon restarts. All Sky emits changed from `app.emit()` to `app.emit_to(\"main\")` for targeted delivery. Stale `CHANNEL_REGISTRY` entries are drained when a new Cocoon channel opens.\n\nAlso strip boilerplate doc sections (Dependencies, Dependents, VSCode Pattern Reference, Thread Safety, Error Handling Strategy) from IPC module doc comments and replace uniformative `/// fn`/`/// Data for struct` with actual descriptions across ~400 files.",
			"SHA": "d592c9a7674e4b31ea27a36b59f1a77f574a536a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T18:56:13Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1858,
				29
			],
			"Message": "docs(Mountain): Strip meta prefixes and TODO stubs from doc comments\n\nReplace \"Delegates to X module\" doc stubs on FileSystemProvider trait method\nimpls with concrete descriptions of each operation. Remove \"This struct...\",\n\"This function...\", and \"Represents...\" meta-instructional prefixes from\ndoc comments across IPC modules (Connection, Encryption, Message, Permission,\nSecurity, TauriIPCServer, ConfigurationBridge, WindAdvancedSync). Strip stale\nTODO-item stubs from MessageCompressor, SecureChannel, Compress, DefineMessage,\nEncrypt, RouteMessage, Types, LogEvent, Permission, Role, and Server modules.\n\nAdd variant-level docs to WebviewLifecycleState enum and enhanced wire-format\ndocs to UriParsing utility. Fix two DTO line continuations in\nExtensionDescriptionStateDTO and WebviewStateDTO.\n\nAlso refactor fix_rustdocs.py and rewrite_docs.py: consolidate regex patterns,\ninline get_pub_items, deduplicate split_pascal, remove unused imports, rename\nhelpers for clarity (fix_meta_instructional → fix_meta, pascal_to_verb_phrase\n→ pascal_to_verb).",
			"SHA": "33842cc9a1b2153326621c1afd245c523445c6a8"
		},
